-- title:
--   Polynomial separating an absent eigensystem from a Hecke maximal ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a discrete valuation domain with residue field $k =$ `ResidueField 𝒪`, let $M \ge 1$ and let $S \subseteq \mathbb N$. Here [`CohCarrier.H1 M ⊤ A`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L162) is the group of additive homomorphisms $\Gamma_0(M) \to A$ (the group `GammaH M ⊤` inside $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)$), [`CohCarrier.Gen M S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) is the inductive type of formal generators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid M$), $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q \mid M$) and $\langle d\rangle$ ($d \in (\mathbb Z/M)^\times$), and [`CohCarrier.opFamily`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) sends these to the endomorphisms `heckeTL` at $\ell$ resp. $q$ (restriction along `conjL`, conjugation by $\mathrm{diag}(1,\ell)$ on $\Gamma_0(M) \cap \Gamma^0(\ell)$, followed by the transfer) and to the diamond operator `diamondL`. Assume `hcomm`, that these operators on $H^1(M,\mathcal O)$ commute pairwise, and fix $\bar\theta :$ `Gen M S` $\to k$; together these form [`CohCarrier.hdata`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L96), whose `opSubalgebra` is the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra $\mathbb T = \mathcal O[\mathrm{range}\ \mathrm{op}] \subseteq \mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O} H^1(M,\mathcal O)$ generated by the operators. Let `Sp` be an `IdempotentSplitting` of $\mathbb T$: an $n$, complete orthogonal idempotents $e_i$ and maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_i$ ($i \in$ `Fin n`) exhausting the maximal ideals of $\mathbb T$, with $e_i \in \mathfrak m_j$ iff $i \ne j$. Let $\iota$ be a type, $\ell : \iota \to \mathbb N$ with each $\ell i$ prime, $\ell i \notin S$, $\ell i \nmid M$, and $c : \iota \to k$, and assume every $v \in H^1(M,k)$ with `heckeT` at $\ell i$ acting on $v$ as $c_i \cdot v$ for all $i$ vanishes. Then for each $i_0 \in$ `Fin n` there is $f \in \mathcal O[\iota]$ with $f(c) = 0$ in $k$ while the value of $f$ at the family of Hecke operators $T_{\ell i} \in \mathbb T$ does not lie in $\mathfrak m_{i_0}$.
--
--   This is the elementary half of the dictionary between maximal ideals of the Hecke algebra acting on $H^1(\Gamma_0(M),\mathcal O)$ and systems of residual Hecke eigenvalues occurring in $H^1(\Gamma_0(M),k)$: a system not occurring is separated from each maximal ideal by a polynomial in the good Hecke operators. It is used in the construction of corner realisations at levels divisible by an auxiliary prime, where the separating polynomial produces the element of the Hecke algebra killing the unwanted component.
